- op: discuss  # a309
  at: '2026-04-07T18:25:08Z'  # a309
  by: agent  # a309
  actor: jgstern_agent  # a309
  clock: 10  # a309
  nonce: a309  # a309
  message: "VALIDATED via deep-20260407-050552 iter-002 (post-WI-saful PR #2762).\n\nEvidence (dataflow_slice_ratio iter-001 → iter-002):\n  alertmanager: 0.166 → 0.246 (+48%)\n  kserve:       0.543 → 0.629 (+16%)\n  prometheus:   0.060 → 0.090 (+49%)\n\nThe forward dataflow slice is now substantially larger across all three cohort repos. The original INV-sabum claim — that propagating access_mode to dispatches_to/uses edges was needed to fix LOW_DATAFLOW_SLICE_RATIO — is empirically refuted. The actual fix was at the slice BFS level (admit one-hop downstream reads from writers), not at the linker level. Dispatches_to edges continue to be followed via graceful degradation (unannotated edges are still followed in dataflow mode by design), and the WI-saful one-hop rule means writer chains now reach reader-side terminals via direct write→read transitions.\n\nWI-hukoh tracks the longer-term option (2)/(3) decision (dest_access_mode population vs. stateful per-node writer-chain BFS). That work is no longer urgent for this bakeoff signal but remains a structural cleanup opportunity."  # a309
